    <p>
      i'm lecheeel — a developer who mostly builds things for myself, then
      reluctantly shares them.
    </p>
    <p>current obsessions:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <a href="https://github.com/Lecheeel/memento" target="_blank" rel="noopener">memento</a>
        — a notification → memory pipeline that turns phone noise into something
        an AI can actually use
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href="https://github.com/Lecheeel/worldline-engine" target="_blank" rel="noopener">worldline-engine</a>
        — a deterministic, replayable multi-agent simulation kernel
      </li>
      <li>self-hosting a personal agent on a 1.6GB VPS and keeping it from falling over</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      i write about the parts that surprised me — those are the only ones worth
